Rebirth in the Silence｜Complete Location Edition

1. The Protagonist’s Revival: Becoming a PodCast Host
The protagonist has endured a long period of despair,
with both life and spirit sinking into silence.

One day, a seasoned PodCast host—acting as a mentor—
recognizes something compelling in the protagonist’s voice.

“Why don’t you create your own show?”

For the first time, the protagonist’s voice is acknowledged as work.

The show gradually gains listeners,
leading to monetization → financial recovery → emotional recovery.

Seeking a symbol of rebirth,
the protagonist travels to Milan.

2. Milan: The Protagonist’s New Suit
In Milan, the protagonist visits a historic tailoring brand
and purchases the first truly authentic suit of his life.

This suit becomes a symbolic item in the narrative,
with potential brand collaboration after the film’s release.

Wearing the suit, the protagonist feels
the unmistakable beginning of a new self.

3. Japan Location Route (Silence × City × Recovery)
After reclaiming a new identity in Milan,
the protagonist travels to Japan in search of quietude.

3-1. Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building Observation Deck (Shinjuku)
Role: Gateway to Urban Silence

The protagonist visits the observation deck wearing the new suit.
From 202 meters above ground, he gazes across Tokyo and realizes:

“I’m still alive. The world is vast.”

3-2. Kumano Shrine (Shinjuku)
Role: Kindness Within the City

A few minutes’ walk from the massive government building,
the protagonist suddenly enters a pocket of silence.

This shrine echoes the kindness he once felt in Shinjuku,
symbolizing the contrast between noise and stillness.

3-3. Hie Shrine (Akasaka)
Role: Boundary Between Power and Prayer

Located beside the National Diet Building,
Hie Shrine represents quietude at the edge of political power.

The protagonist climbs the stairs in his suit,
reflecting on social structures and his place within them.

3-4. Ohtori Shrine (Meguro – Tori no Ichi Festival)
Role: Urban Heat × Moment of Recovery

The protagonist arrives during the vibrant Tori no Ichi festival.
Amid waves of people, lantern lights, and festival sounds,
he encounters the warmth and energy of the city.

Here, he fully regains his strength.

This festival sequence is expected to draw global attention
after the film’s release.

4. Osorezan (Aomori)｜Deepest Layer of Silence
Role: The Abyss of the Narrative

Osorezan stands at the end of the urban silence route,
embodying the quietude of life and death.

The protagonist removes his suit,
walking the land in a more honest, unguarded state.

Wind, the lake, sulfur, prayer, and the boundary between worlds
resonate with the protagonist’s inner ocean.

Here, he quietly accepts:

“Life, death, and forgiveness.”

